WEBVTT

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.172
Hmm...

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.510
Hmm... There.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:17.516
Excellent.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.950
You recognized
the complementary base pair.

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:23.784
Actually, I just found
two pieces that fit together.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.381
You're missing
the point.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.426
I thought the point
was to finish the puzzle.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.325
And learn something
about genetics.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.523
If you really want to help,

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:35.466
find me a green piece
that looks like Tuvok's ear.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.366
Commander.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.133
At ease.
I'm just passing through.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.798
I apologize

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.309
for the condition
of the cargo bay, sir.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.901
I've been
tutoring Naomi.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.640
Looks like you found
a creative approach.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.806
Thank you, but I'd

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.577
appreciate it
if you didn't tell Seven.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.184
I'm supposed
to be writing a paper

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.483
on transwarp instability.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.750
Don't worry,
your secret's safe...

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.519
as long as you keep mine.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:00.889
Sir?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.222
Antarian cider.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.263
Not the replicated stuff.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.355
There are only
a couple of bottles left,

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.867
and I don't want Mr. Neelix
getting his hands on them.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.300
Well, then you should store them

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.133
with the salvaged
Borg components.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:15.470
Neelix never inventories
those containers.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.339
He says they give him
the creeps.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.537
Officer-level thinking, Icheb.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.704
Would you mind?

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.270
Of course not.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.926
Come in.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.358
You're late.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.457
Unfortunately, so's dinner.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.968
Let me guess...
you burned the roast again.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.197
Once, a long time ago,

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.638
I called this replicator
a glorified toaster.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:49.970
It never forgave me.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:54.980
I didn't realize
replicators held grudges.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.709
What's so funny?

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.444
I just left Icheb and Naomi

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.351
assembling a jigsaw
puzzle in the cargo bay.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.322
Find me the thermal
regulator, please.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.687
How is Icheb?

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:09.057
In a few years, he may
be running the ship.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.596
I don't know about you,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.358
but I'm not ready
to retire just yet.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.560
Janeway to the Bridge. Report.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.127
That was some kind
of gravimetric surge.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.298
It's overloading
our inertial dampeners.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.363
Source?

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.568
That's a good question.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.203
Seven's trying to localize it.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.616
Engineering says the warp core
is destabilizing.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.809
I'd better get down there.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.186
A spatial rift is opening
directly in front of us.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.286
It's emitting high levels
of neutrinos and chronitons.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.591
On screen.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.365
What is it?

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.904
I don't know.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.401
We're losing containment.
Everyone out!

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.763
Torres to the Transporter Room.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:22.062
Beam Commander Chakotay
directly to Sick Bay, now!

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.443
Welcome back.

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:19.251
Lie still.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.451
What happened?

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.547
You were transported here.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.922
Your body was
in a state of temporal flux.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.891
Temporal flux?

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.724
You had the liver
of an 80-year-old man

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.424
and the kidneys
of a 12-year-old boy.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.799
Fortunately,
I was able to create

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.199
a chroniton-infused serum

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.465
that you brought you back
into temporal alignment.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.905
Anywhere else,

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.568
that antidote would have
earned me a prestigious award.

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:47.112
Of course, on Voyager,
it's just another day

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:50.377
in the life of an
under-appreciated EMH.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.849
What about the
rest of the crew?

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:52.907
No other casualties?

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:53.952
Not that I'm aware of.

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.315
I've tried
calling the Bridge,

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:56.685
but no one answers.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.950
Were we attacked?

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.581
I don't think so.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:03.493
We ran into some
sort of anomaly.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:08.030
Naturally, no one
thought to inform me.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:09.432
What do you think
you're doing?

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:10.434
Leaving.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.663
And you're going with me.

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:12.670
I am?

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:14.172
There may be other
injured crewmen.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.172
In case you've forgotten,

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:17.471
I'm a prisoner of these walls.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.805
Where's your mobile emitter?

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.106
My what?

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:24.481
I'll be back.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.482
Wait.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:28.111
Tell me about this...
mobile emitter.

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:36.285
Bridge.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:55.942
Harry...

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:56.947
what's going on?

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:57.948
Sir?

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.848
I'm afraid I don't know you.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.011
Take him into custody.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:05.121
How did you get aboard
this ship?

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:07.724
Kathryn...

00:07:07.794 --> 00:07:10.888
Oh, I didn't realize
we were on a first-name basis.

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:11.987
We should have known

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.656
that the Maquis were involved.

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:15.166
Maquis?

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.201
Involved in what?

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.667
Just when we're about
to chase your ship

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:20.763
into the Badlands,

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.535
our systems start malfunctioning

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.508
and you step off the turbolift.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.611
Captain, I know this
may be hard to believe,

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.149
but I think I've somehow

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:34.015
been thrown seven years
into Voyager's past.

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:35.883
Really?

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.513
Let's try another theory.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:40.787
You learned Voyager had been
assigned to capture you,

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.829
and you managed to get
on board to sabotage her.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.727
Check your sensors.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:48.232
See if they're showing
any strange temporal readings.

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:50.929
Captain, the environmental
controls are fluctuating.

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:54.568
Take him to the brig.

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:09.118
Halt turbolift.

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.917
Engineering.

00:08:17.063 --> 00:08:18.030
Seska.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.007
Hold him still.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:40.444
You didn't really think
I'd hurt you, did you?

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:44.854
How'd you get here?

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:46.186
Don't tell me
that little bump

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:48.284
on your head
gave you amnesia.

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:49.328
It's time you accepted

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:51.295
that I'm in control
of Voyager now.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.326
That was five years ago.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.266
What are you talking about?

00:08:57.336 --> 00:09:00.305
Listen, Seska, there's
some kind of temporal anomaly

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:01.340
going on here.

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.399
I want to know how many more

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:04.773
of your people
are back on board.

00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:10.006
All right, I'll tell you.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:11.481
I've got a dozen officers
with me.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.882
We've already locked you out

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:13.883
of every key system.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:14.884
In less than an hour,

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:16.989
we'll be in control again.

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:19.820
In less than a minute,
you're going to be dead,

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:22.360
if you don't give me
access to those systems.

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:26.761
I'll need to use that console.

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:32.268
Just don't do anything
you'll regret.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.307
Move.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.282
Stop him!

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.444
Warning. Coolant system breach.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:51.189
Don't make me kill you.

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:05.461
No.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:06.766
Scan the perimeter.

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:09.034
Report any anomalous readings.

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:10.507
There's something wrong here.

00:10:25.224 --> 00:10:28.853
Whoever you are,
I suggest you surrender.

00:10:28.928 --> 00:10:29.895
I'm armed!

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:32.362
It's only me, Doc.

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:33.398
Commander.

00:10:34.867 --> 00:10:36.596
Please tell me what's going on.

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:38.068
If you tell me the stardate.

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:39.695
49624.

00:10:39.772 --> 00:10:42.605
No wonder you didn't know
about the mobile emitter.

00:10:42.675 --> 00:10:44.302
You don't get it
for another year.

00:10:44.377 --> 00:10:45.639
I don't understand.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:47.645
I'm not sure
I get it myself,

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:49.806
but the ship seems
to have been fractured somehow.

00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:51.144
Fractured?

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.981
Different areas seem to exist
in different time periods.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.452
How many of these
"time periods" are there?

00:10:56.522 --> 00:10:57.454
I'm not sure.

00:10:57.523 --> 00:11:00.492
On the Bridge,
it's before Voyager

00:11:00.559 --> 00:11:01.651
even left the Alpha Quadrant.

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:03.092
In Engineering, it's the time

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:05.187
when the Kazon
took over the ship.

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:07.357
Kazon? We've got
to protect ourselves.

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:09.298
Don't worry.
So far, I'm the only one

00:11:09.368 --> 00:11:11.461
who can cross
from one zone into another.

00:11:11.537 --> 00:11:13.027
That serum you gave me...

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:16.268
it must have
made me immune.

00:11:16.342 --> 00:11:19.140
Normal technology won't
pass through the barriers.

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:20.439
Can you replicate

00:11:20.513 --> 00:11:23.243
a chroniton-infused
hypospray casing,

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:25.545
using the same principles
you used to make the serum?

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:26.880
I think so. Why?

00:11:26.952 --> 00:11:28.783
I have to take
some of it with me.

00:11:28.854 --> 00:11:29.912
What for?

00:11:29.989 --> 00:11:32.389
If I'm going to put the
ship back together again,

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:33.425
I need help.

00:11:40.433 --> 00:11:42.333
Captain.

00:11:42.401 --> 00:11:44.892
Where are my officers?

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.666
The turbolift passed
through a temporal barrier.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.765
They couldn't get through.

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:50.900
If you're willing
to hear me out,

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:52.443
I can explain...
at least partly.

00:11:52.511 --> 00:11:55.173
You mean about your being
from the future?

00:11:55.247 --> 00:11:58.478
Your first Starfleet posting
was on the Al-Batani,

00:11:58.551 --> 00:12:01.486
where you once knocked out power
to six decks

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:03.454
by misaligning
the positronic relays.

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:06.514
Nice try, but you could
have read that

00:12:06.592 --> 00:12:09.186
in the Maquis intelligence file.

00:12:09.295 --> 00:12:11.388
How's Molly,

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:13.591
your Irish setter?

00:12:13.666 --> 00:12:16.134
You rescued her
from a pound on Taris Seti IV.

00:12:16.202 --> 00:12:18.830
She was the runt of the litter,
but you thought she had spunk.

00:12:18.904 --> 00:12:22.271
You love music,
but you never learned

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:25.105
to play an instrument...
something you still regret.

00:12:25.177 --> 00:12:27.702
How do you know these things?

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.978
Because you told me,
about three years from now.

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:36.483
My ready room.

00:12:46.465 --> 00:12:50.060
It's a fascinating story,
but as the Ferengi say,

00:12:50.136 --> 00:12:53.970
"A good lie is easier to believe
than the truth."

00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:55.903
So you're saying
no one on your crew

00:12:55.975 --> 00:12:58.341
has encountered
one of these temporal barriers?

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.707
My helmsman disappeared

00:12:59.779 --> 00:13:02.179
when she tried
to walk down that corridor,

00:13:02.248 --> 00:13:04.580
but that doesn't prove
she passed through

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.912
a temporal barrier.

00:13:06.051 --> 00:13:09.111
If you inject yourself, I can
take you down that corridor

00:13:09.188 --> 00:13:11.918
and show you everything
that I've said is true.

00:13:12.057 --> 00:13:15.549
Have Mr. Kim run
a full-spectral analysis.

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:17.220
For all I know, this is poison

00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:21.392
and Mr. Chakotay is trying
to assassinate me.

00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:22.900
She's right.

00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:26.460
It's poison, and I'll use it.

00:13:33.879 --> 00:13:36.439
Let her go.

00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:38.176
Lower your weapon.

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:42.015
Captain!

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.951
Andrews to the Bridge.

00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:47.252
I need help here.

00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:48.258
Andrews!

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:49.692
He can't hear you.

00:13:49.762 --> 00:13:51.957
We've moved into
a different time frame.

00:13:52.031 --> 00:13:54.966
Scan the area, but don't
go past that bulkhead.

00:13:55.067 --> 00:13:57.763
You want more proof?
It's right down that corridor.

00:13:57.837 --> 00:13:59.498
You just have to trust me.

00:13:59.572 --> 00:14:02.166
It isn't easy
when you're holding me hostage.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:07.911
Stay or go... it's your choice.

00:14:08.047 --> 00:14:09.810
Now that I'm inoculated,

00:14:09.882 --> 00:14:12.851
I can go anywhere
on the ship I want.

00:14:12.918 --> 00:14:14.283
That's right.

00:14:14.353 --> 00:14:17.220
Then I suppose I don't
need you anymore.

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:20.884
Without me, you'll be
walking into a future

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.928
you know nothing about.

00:14:22.995 --> 00:14:24.155
Where are we going?

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.595
The Astrometrics Lab.

00:14:25.664 --> 00:14:28.064
Voyager doesn't have
an Astrometrics Lab.

00:14:28.133 --> 00:14:30.624
Harry designed it...
or will design it.

00:14:30.703 --> 00:14:32.364
Harry Kim?

00:14:32.438 --> 00:14:34.030
I realize,
from your perspective,

00:14:34.106 --> 00:14:35.095
he's new to the job,

00:14:35.174 --> 00:14:37.938
but he's going to become
one of our best people.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:40.342
Deck 8.

00:14:40.412 --> 00:14:41.811
"Our" people?

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:44.441
I'm going to be
your First Officer.

00:14:44.516 --> 00:14:45.949
Really?

00:14:46.018 --> 00:14:50.648
What's the reason we're
going to this, uh, Astrometrics?

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:53.157
It has temporal sensors
that can help us map the ship

00:14:53.225 --> 00:14:56.388
and tell us how many
time frames we're dealing with.

00:14:56.462 --> 00:14:58.054
Now you're trying to tell me

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.155
Harry Kim invented
temporal sensors?

00:15:00.232 --> 00:15:03.895
No. We used Borg technology
for that.

00:15:04.036 --> 00:15:05.230
Borg?

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:07.135
It's a long story.

00:15:07.206 --> 00:15:09.868
Maybe you better keep it
to yourself.

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:12.868
The Temporal Prime Directive.

00:15:12.945 --> 00:15:15.175
The less I know about
the future, the better.

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.554
She's got a pulse.

00:15:27.059 --> 00:15:30.153
I'm detecting
an active neurogenic field.

00:15:30.229 --> 00:15:32.390
This could be the day
the telepathic pitcher plant

00:15:32.464 --> 00:15:34.329
put us all into comas.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.527
Or it might be the time
aliens invaded our dreams.

00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:38.627
We've got to get them help.

00:15:38.704 --> 00:15:39.636
Don't worry.

00:15:39.705 --> 00:15:42.265
We managed to get out
of both situations.

00:15:57.990 --> 00:15:59.423
Captain?

00:15:59.491 --> 00:16:00.958
I'm sorry...

00:16:01.093 --> 00:16:03.220
I don't recognize you,
Lieutenant.

00:16:03.295 --> 00:16:07.095
It's me... Naomi Wildman.

00:16:07.166 --> 00:16:09.498
How did you?

00:16:09.568 --> 00:16:10.830
Are you Icheb?

00:16:10.903 --> 00:16:12.427
Yes.

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:15.701
Something tells me
you weren't expecting us.

00:16:15.774 --> 00:16:17.207
No, ma'am.

00:16:17.276 --> 00:16:19.267
You both died...

00:16:19.345 --> 00:16:20.744
17 years ago.

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:30.018
The Captain and I
haven't risen from the grave.

00:16:30.089 --> 00:16:32.922
The ship's been fractured
into different time frames.

00:16:33.058 --> 00:16:34.548
37, to be exact.

00:16:34.626 --> 00:16:36.059
How did you calculate that?

00:16:36.128 --> 00:16:39.825
We've had 17 years
to upgrade the sensors.

00:16:39.898 --> 00:16:42.765
A chronokinetic surge
interacted with the warp core.

00:16:42.835 --> 00:16:45.395
It shattered the space-time
continuum aboard the ship.

00:16:45.471 --> 00:16:47.871
The accident that occurred
in your time frame.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.100
The question is:

00:16:49.174 --> 00:16:52.234
Can we repair the damage?

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:54.370
If we could get
to a section of the ship

00:16:54.446 --> 00:16:56.380
that still exists
in that time period,

00:16:56.448 --> 00:16:58.279
maybe we could
counteract the surge,

00:16:58.350 --> 00:16:59.749
stop it from happening.

00:16:59.818 --> 00:17:02.844
That section was
the focal point of the surge.

00:17:02.921 --> 00:17:06.118
It seems to have been...
obliterated.

00:17:07.593 --> 00:17:09.527
It's too bad
Seven's not here.

00:17:09.595 --> 00:17:11.529
Seven?

00:17:11.597 --> 00:17:12.757
Someone who knows more

00:17:12.831 --> 00:17:14.890
about temporal mechanics
than any of us.

00:17:15.034 --> 00:17:18.231
Unfortunately, she hasn't
been found, either.

00:17:18.303 --> 00:17:20.897
Maybe we can find her
in another time frame.

00:17:21.006 --> 00:17:23.702
I have an Ensign
Samantha Wildman on my crew.

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:26.040
My mother.

00:17:26.111 --> 00:17:28.909
Naomi was the first
child born on Voyager.

00:17:29.014 --> 00:17:32.745
A few years later,
we rescued Icheb from the Borg.

00:17:32.818 --> 00:17:36.219
When I was little,
there was nothing I wanted more

00:17:36.288 --> 00:17:39.086
than to be the
Assistant Captain.

00:17:39.158 --> 00:17:42.787
We should get moving.

00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:43.623
Commander.

00:17:45.197 --> 00:17:46.926
In case you were wondering,

00:17:46.999 --> 00:17:50.093
I never told Neelix
where you hid that cider.

00:17:59.645 --> 00:18:01.738
So why are we
looking for this...

00:18:01.814 --> 00:18:03.304
Seven in the cargo bay?

00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:05.077
She spent a lot
of time there.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:06.276
Working?

00:18:06.351 --> 00:18:08.251
Regenerating.

00:18:17.629 --> 00:18:20.462
Maybe you'd better fill me in.

00:18:23.836 --> 00:18:25.360
This looks like the time

00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:28.270
you forged a temporary
alliance with the Borg.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.467
What's happened
to this vessel?

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:35.810
Captain Janeway...
meet Seven of Nine...

00:18:35.881 --> 00:18:37.712
Tertiary Adjunct

00:18:37.783 --> 00:18:39.410
of Unimatrix Zero One.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.212
When a Borg cube travels
through a transwarp corridor,

00:18:44.289 --> 00:18:45.916
the temporal stresses
are extreme.

00:18:46.058 --> 00:18:48.925
To keep the different sections
of the cube in temporal sync,

00:18:49.027 --> 00:18:52.053
we project a chroniton field
throughout the vessel.

00:18:52.131 --> 00:18:53.928
How?

00:18:54.066 --> 00:18:56.500
Each cube has
specially designed conduits.

00:18:56.568 --> 00:18:59.731
If we install similar conduits
throughout this vessel

00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:02.638
then generate
a sufficiently powerful field,

00:19:02.708 --> 00:19:05.734
we may be able to force Voyager
back into temporal sync.

00:19:05.811 --> 00:19:08.211
Temporal sync with what?

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:10.544
The vessel will return
to the moment

00:19:10.616 --> 00:19:12.880
of the original
chronokinetic surge.

00:19:13.018 --> 00:19:15.220
Since the surge will last
for six to seven seconds,

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.517
Since the surge will last
for six to seven seconds,

00:19:16.588 --> 00:19:18.556
Commander Chakotay
will have a short time

00:19:18.624 --> 00:19:21.422
in which to try to counteract
the warp core reaction.

00:19:21.493 --> 00:19:23.518
Even if we could replicate
these conduits,

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:26.587
we'd have no way to get them
through the temporal barriers.

00:19:26.665 --> 00:19:29.600
The bio-neural circuitry.

00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:30.828
Captain?

00:19:30.903 --> 00:19:32.894
It runs through every
section of the ship,

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:34.404
almost like
a nervous system.

00:19:34.473 --> 00:19:36.703
If we could inject
the gel packs

00:19:36.775 --> 00:19:39.209
with your serum,
we could use them

00:19:39.278 --> 00:19:41.337
to transmit
the chroniton field.

00:19:41.413 --> 00:19:43.176
The warp core
could be recalibrated

00:19:43.248 --> 00:19:44.579
to generate that field.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:46.140
Work on it.

00:19:46.218 --> 00:19:49.119
Chakotay and I will see
about modifying the serum.

00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:50.450
Your plan is inefficient.

00:19:50.522 --> 00:19:52.114
Why?

00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:53.283
There are only two of you.

00:19:53.358 --> 00:19:54.450
If I were to assimilate you

00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:55.652
into a small Borg collective,

00:19:55.727 --> 00:19:57.058
you could then
assimilate others.

00:19:57.129 --> 00:19:59.825
The work would proceed
more quickly.

00:19:59.898 --> 00:20:02.526
Sorry, but I like
my plan better.

00:20:02.601 --> 00:20:03.898
We'll be back.

00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:14.178
That was an interesting
experience.

00:20:14.246 --> 00:20:16.146
If it makes you
feel any better,

00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:17.477
you're going to develop
quite a knack

00:20:17.549 --> 00:20:18.516
for dealing
with the Borg.

00:20:18.584 --> 00:20:20.415
You mean we're going
to be seeing more of them?

00:20:20.485 --> 00:20:22.953
We'll run into them
on a few occasions.

00:20:23.088 --> 00:20:25.648
Why do I get the feeling
that's an understatement?

00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:28.249
It doesn't seem
like my first command

00:20:28.327 --> 00:20:30.591
is shaping up
the way I expected.

00:20:30.662 --> 00:20:33.961
"In the middle of the
journey of our life,

00:20:34.032 --> 00:20:36.865
"I found myself astray
in a dark wood

00:20:36.935 --> 00:20:40.496
where the straight
road had been lost."

00:20:40.572 --> 00:20:45.236
I didn't know Dante's Inferno
was on the Maquis reading list.

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:48.177
Actually, I borrowed your copy.

00:20:48.247 --> 00:20:51.341
My fiancé gave me that book
as an engagement gift.

00:20:51.416 --> 00:20:53.384
I've never lent it to anyone.

00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:55.079
Not yet.

00:20:55.153 --> 00:20:58.179
Anyway, I agree with Dante.

00:20:58.257 --> 00:21:00.657
If you always see
the road ahead of you,

00:21:00.726 --> 00:21:02.421
it's not worth the trip.

00:21:02.494 --> 00:21:06.089
A soldier and a philosopher.

00:21:06.164 --> 00:21:10.191
Your intelligence file
doesn't do you justice.

00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:13.067
I've replicated these belts
to resist the effects

00:21:13.138 --> 00:21:15.868
of the temporal barriers,
just like the hyposprays.

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:18.910
I didn't realize you were
programmed to be so versatile.

00:21:18.977 --> 00:21:20.672
I wasn't, but when
you are thrown

00:21:20.746 --> 00:21:22.373
into the deep end
of the galaxy

00:21:22.447 --> 00:21:24.642
and left running
for as long as I've been,

00:21:24.716 --> 00:21:27.241
it helps to develop
a few extra subroutines.

00:21:27.319 --> 00:21:28.946
How long have you
been running?

00:21:29.021 --> 00:21:30.249
Almost three years...

00:21:30.322 --> 00:21:32.654
since our original
Doctor was killed.

00:21:32.724 --> 00:21:34.316
Killed? How?

00:21:34.393 --> 00:21:37.055
In the incident that stranded us
here in the Delta Qua...

00:21:37.129 --> 00:21:39.097
Doctor.

00:21:40.699 --> 00:21:43.827
The Temporal Prime
Directive... remember?

00:21:43.902 --> 00:21:45.733
Of course.

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:49.501
I'm sorry.

00:21:49.574 --> 00:21:50.768
The Delta Quadrant?

00:21:50.842 --> 00:21:52.901
Is that what he
was about to say?

00:21:52.978 --> 00:21:54.206
Ready?

00:21:55.914 --> 00:21:58.849
I'll take the upper decks;
you take the lower.

00:21:58.917 --> 00:22:01.477
I don't think splitting up's
a good idea.

00:22:01.553 --> 00:22:02.918
We'll get the job done faster.

00:22:02.988 --> 00:22:04.148
As your First Officer,

00:22:04.222 --> 00:22:05.484
it's my duty to protect you.

00:22:05.557 --> 00:22:07.787
I know a lot more about
what's out there than you do,

00:22:07.859 --> 00:22:09.349
and we have no way
of communicating

00:22:09.428 --> 00:22:10.827
if something goes wrong.

00:22:10.896 --> 00:22:13.660
It may take a little longer,
but we should go together.

00:22:14.733 --> 00:22:17.531
After you...

00:22:17.602 --> 00:22:18.864
Commander.

00:22:34.753 --> 00:22:37.313
Can I ask you something?

00:22:37.389 --> 00:22:40.415
I started off
with a crew of 153.

00:22:40.492 --> 00:22:42.960
I already know
I lost my Doctor.

00:22:43.095 --> 00:22:44.687
How many others?

00:22:44.763 --> 00:22:48.665
We'll suffer casualties
like any other starship,

00:22:48.734 --> 00:22:51.635
but you'll also gain
new crewmen as well.

00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:53.398
Like you.

00:22:53.472 --> 00:22:55.702
How do you get to be
my First Officer?

00:22:55.774 --> 00:22:58.402
Our crews will be
forced to work together

00:22:58.477 --> 00:22:59.910
after we get stranded.

00:22:59.978 --> 00:23:01.912
In the Delta Quadrant?

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:03.811
How does that happen?

00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:07.477
Are you sure
you want to know?

00:23:16.294 --> 00:23:18.558
Run!

00:23:23.535 --> 00:23:25.901
What the hell was that?

00:23:25.971 --> 00:23:27.939
A macrovirus...
they infected the ship

00:23:28.039 --> 00:23:30.507
a few years ago.

00:23:30.575 --> 00:23:32.338
It sounds like it's going to be

00:23:32.411 --> 00:23:34.743
one disaster after another
on this ship.

00:23:34.813 --> 00:23:36.644
You once told me
that Starfleet Captains

00:23:36.715 --> 00:23:39.206
don't choose their missions,
the missions choose them.

00:23:39.284 --> 00:23:41.684
You're going to have
the opportunity to study things

00:23:41.753 --> 00:23:43.152
no human has ever seen before.

00:23:43.221 --> 00:23:47.021
Including some very large germs.

00:23:56.001 --> 00:23:58.970
A monochromatic environment?

00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:00.970
It's called black and white.

00:24:01.072 --> 00:24:03.905
It's one of Tom Paris'
holodeck programs.

00:24:03.975 --> 00:24:07.775
He based it on some old
science fiction serials.

00:24:07.846 --> 00:24:09.905
Interesting technology.

00:24:09.981 --> 00:24:11.915
Captain Proton's rocket pack.

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:13.915
Captain Proton?

00:24:14.052 --> 00:24:15.747
The savior of the universe.

00:24:15.821 --> 00:24:19.018
Doesn't sound like Mr. Paris'
tastes are very sophisticated.

00:24:19.090 --> 00:24:21.320
That's why we love
having him around.

00:24:21.393 --> 00:24:23.861
The access port
should be in there.

00:24:40.879 --> 00:24:43.143
Here. I think
I found the panel.

00:24:43.215 --> 00:24:44.910
Give me a hand.

00:24:49.488 --> 00:24:50.887
Halt

00:24:50.956 --> 00:24:52.924
in the name of Chaotica!

00:24:52.991 --> 00:24:54.424
Seize them!

00:24:54.493 --> 00:24:55.425
Oh, no.

00:24:55.494 --> 00:24:56.756
Computer, deactivate program.

00:24:56.828 --> 00:24:58.090
Unable to comply.

00:24:58.163 --> 00:24:59.095
Surrender.

00:24:59.164 --> 00:25:00.290
Holodeck controls are off-line.

00:25:00.365 --> 00:25:01.525
Hold on.

00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:02.828
Now, wait a minute.

00:25:02.901 --> 00:25:04.869
Seize! My liege!

00:25:04.936 --> 00:25:06.767
Do not resist.

00:25:06.838 --> 00:25:09.033
They were attempting

00:25:09.107 --> 00:25:11.439
to rob your laboratory!

00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:13.000
Fool!

00:25:13.078 --> 00:25:14.409
Don't you recognize

00:25:14.479 --> 00:25:18.438
the Queen of the Spider People?

00:25:20.385 --> 00:25:25.152
Arachnia... my bride.

00:25:25.223 --> 00:25:30.126
I knew you'd return
to me one day...

00:25:30.195 --> 00:25:33.494
so I could watch you die.

00:25:46.778 --> 00:25:49.645
Raise the lightning shield!

00:25:49.714 --> 00:25:51.944
Power the death ray!

00:25:52.083 --> 00:25:54.574
Her fleet may
be lurking nearby.

00:25:54.653 --> 00:25:56.177
We must defend ourselves.

00:25:56.254 --> 00:25:57.312
I'm open to suggestions.

00:25:57.389 --> 00:26:00.620
Our best bet is to play along.

00:26:00.692 --> 00:26:02.284
Don't let me stop you.

00:26:02.360 --> 00:26:04.089
I'm not the one
he's in love with.

00:26:04.162 --> 00:26:05.891
Arachnia...

00:26:06.031 --> 00:26:10.058
you beguiled me once
with your foul potions.

00:26:10.135 --> 00:26:13.332
Did you think you could toy
with my affections again?

00:26:13.405 --> 00:26:15.896
Were these characters
always this ridiculous?

00:26:15.974 --> 00:26:17.839
If I order Lonzak

00:26:17.909 --> 00:26:19.843
to pull that lever,

00:26:19.911 --> 00:26:21.105
you'll never mock me again.

00:26:24.015 --> 00:26:25.812
Arachnia.

00:26:26.885 --> 00:26:30.582
Please, my liege.

00:26:30.655 --> 00:26:33.488
I meant it was ridiculous

00:26:33.558 --> 00:26:36.686
to think I would
ever try to deceive you.

00:26:36.761 --> 00:26:39.628
I've come to warn you

00:26:39.698 --> 00:26:42.030
of a fiendish plot.

00:26:43.101 --> 00:26:46.400
By aliens from
the Eighth Dimension.

00:26:49.741 --> 00:26:51.174
Eighth?

00:26:51.242 --> 00:26:53.676
Everyone knows there are only

00:26:53.745 --> 00:26:55.440
five dimensions.

00:26:58.016 --> 00:26:59.950
If you don't believe us,

00:27:00.085 --> 00:27:03.316
examine their handiwork
for yourself.

00:27:03.388 --> 00:27:05.652
There's a hidden panel
over there,

00:27:05.724 --> 00:27:08.386
behind those rocks.

00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:09.757
Very well.

00:27:09.828 --> 00:27:11.728
I'll humor you.

00:27:11.796 --> 00:27:13.024
Lonzak!

00:27:20.939 --> 00:27:22.804
I've found it, Highness!

00:27:22.874 --> 00:27:25.308
They've sabotaged my laboratory.

00:27:25.377 --> 00:27:27.072
That vial you're holding...

00:27:27.145 --> 00:27:29.443
it's a neutralizing potion.

00:27:29.514 --> 00:27:31.778
If you inject their device,

00:27:31.850 --> 00:27:34.216
you'll render it harmless.

00:27:43.662 --> 00:27:45.220
Release me,

00:27:45.296 --> 00:27:48.231
and I'll disarm
all their devices...

00:27:48.299 --> 00:27:49.100
throughout your realm.

00:27:49.100 --> 00:27:50.158
Throughout your realm.

00:27:50.235 --> 00:27:53.602
Oh, Arachnia.

00:27:53.672 --> 00:27:56.470
You do love me.

00:27:59.477 --> 00:28:00.739
How could I resist

00:28:00.812 --> 00:28:03.872
your... magnetism?

00:28:03.948 --> 00:28:06.246
Or I, yours.

00:28:06.317 --> 00:28:10.151
Together, we'll rule the cosmos

00:28:10.221 --> 00:28:13.588
and grind our enemies into dust.

00:28:18.496 --> 00:28:20.430
If we restore the timeline,

00:28:20.498 --> 00:28:23.934
remind me to cancel Mr. Paris'
holodeck privileges.

00:28:31.042 --> 00:28:33.203
What the hell's going on?

00:28:33.278 --> 00:28:36.145
And what are you
doing in that uniform?

00:28:36.214 --> 00:28:38.705
It's a little complicated.

00:28:38.783 --> 00:28:41.047
I'm not going anywhere.

00:28:41.119 --> 00:28:45.021
Voyager's had an encounter
with an anomaly.

00:28:45.090 --> 00:28:47.615
It's fractured the ship
into different time periods.

00:28:47.692 --> 00:28:49.216
We're trying to undo the damage,

00:28:49.294 --> 00:28:50.921
but we need access
to that panel.

00:28:53.064 --> 00:28:55.760
First, she destroys our only
way out of the Delta Quadrant,

00:28:55.834 --> 00:28:57.563
and now you're collaborating
with her?

00:28:57.635 --> 00:28:59.034
Try to understand.

00:28:59.104 --> 00:29:01.038
I'm from a time period
in your future

00:29:01.106 --> 00:29:03.165
when all of us
will be working together.

00:29:03.241 --> 00:29:05.072
That's pretty hard to believe.

00:29:05.143 --> 00:29:06.610
B'Elanna, I've never lied

00:29:06.678 --> 00:29:09.647
to you before,
and I'm not lying now.

00:29:30.034 --> 00:29:33.060
That woman blamed me
for stranding Voyager

00:29:33.138 --> 00:29:34.730
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:29:34.806 --> 00:29:36.034
She was angry.

00:29:36.107 --> 00:29:37.597
But was she right?

00:29:37.675 --> 00:29:40.166
You had good reasons
for doing what you did.

00:29:40.245 --> 00:29:41.906
What reasons?

00:29:42.046 --> 00:29:43.775
You were trying to save lives.

00:29:43.848 --> 00:29:46.146
Whose?

00:29:46.217 --> 00:29:48.651
An alien culture, the Ocampans.

00:29:50.955 --> 00:29:53.719
In other words, I'm going
to choose to help strangers

00:29:53.792 --> 00:29:55.487
at the expense
of our own people.

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:57.892
It's not like you
to second-guess yourself.

00:29:57.962 --> 00:30:00.089
In this case,

00:30:00.165 --> 00:30:03.032
I'm second-guessing a decision
I haven't made yet.

00:30:12.510 --> 00:30:14.944
Keep dispensing the netrazine
until we run out,

00:30:15.013 --> 00:30:17.573
then switch to the analeptics.

00:30:17.649 --> 00:30:19.276
Yes, Lieutenant.

00:30:19.350 --> 00:30:20.942
How did you get in here?

00:30:21.085 --> 00:30:22.575
There isn't time to explain.

00:30:22.654 --> 00:30:25.521
What happened
to these people?

00:30:25.590 --> 00:30:27.558
Radiation poisoning.

00:30:27.625 --> 00:30:30.651
The EPS relays overloaded
when we ran into the anomaly.

00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:32.958
We need the Doctor
and medical supplies,

00:30:33.031 --> 00:30:34.965
or we're going to have
a lot more casualties.

00:30:35.066 --> 00:30:36.863
I'm afraid that isn't
possible right now.

00:30:36.935 --> 00:30:38.402
Do the best you can.

00:30:38.469 --> 00:30:41.131
Yes, sir.

00:30:41.206 --> 00:30:44.073
There's an access
panel in the galley.

00:30:55.520 --> 00:30:57.545
Coffee, black.

00:30:57.622 --> 00:31:00.113
How do you know
how I like my coffee?

00:31:00.191 --> 00:31:01.385
Well, you haven't changed

00:31:01.459 --> 00:31:03.290
your standing order
in seven years.

00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:07.195
Thanks, it's just what I needed.

00:31:07.265 --> 00:31:08.892
Don't worry, Captain.

00:31:08.967 --> 00:31:10.764
You'll get us out of this.

00:31:10.835 --> 00:31:12.029
You always do.

00:31:13.104 --> 00:31:14.435
All done here.

00:31:14.505 --> 00:31:16.871
Captain.

00:31:16.941 --> 00:31:18.272
Tuvok?

00:31:24.482 --> 00:31:27.417
I am pleased you are here.

00:31:27.485 --> 00:31:29.146
I didn't think

00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:31.085
I would see you again.

00:31:33.157 --> 00:31:35.182
I want you to know,

00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:38.457
it has been an honor
to serve with you...

00:31:40.565 --> 00:31:43.329
and to be your friend.

00:31:45.069 --> 00:31:47.037
Mr. Paris!

00:31:56.915 --> 00:32:01.011
Live long and prosper.

00:32:30.949 --> 00:32:32.610
Deck 11.

00:32:33.818 --> 00:32:36.446
I can't let this happen,
not again.

00:32:36.521 --> 00:32:38.182
What are you talking about?

00:32:38.256 --> 00:32:40.554
Voyager getting stranded,
all these deaths

00:32:40.625 --> 00:32:42.490
this entire future...
it's my fault.

00:32:42.560 --> 00:32:44.619
I've got to do something
to change it.

00:32:44.696 --> 00:32:46.254
What do you have in mind?

00:32:46.331 --> 00:32:49.129
Maybe we can find a way to
modify Seven of Nine's plan.

00:32:49.200 --> 00:32:51.168
Put Voyager into temporal sync

00:32:51.235 --> 00:32:52.827
- with my time frame.
- Captain...

00:32:52.904 --> 00:32:54.337
Now that I know
what's going to happen,

00:32:54.405 --> 00:32:56.373
I could avoid getting trapped
in the Delta Quadrant

00:32:56.441 --> 00:32:57.669
in the first place.

00:32:57.742 --> 00:32:58.766
Halt turbolift.

00:32:58.843 --> 00:33:00.333
Seven's plan is
dangerous enough.

00:33:00.411 --> 00:33:01.878
Trying to alter it
is too risky.

00:33:01.946 --> 00:33:03.345
It's worth the risk.

00:33:03.414 --> 00:33:04.779
If Seven's idea works,

00:33:04.849 --> 00:33:06.680
Tuvok and those other crewmen
will be fine.

00:33:06.751 --> 00:33:09.219
They'll still be stuck
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:33:09.287 --> 00:33:11.346
If a temporal anomaly
doesn't kill them,

00:33:11.422 --> 00:33:13.185
something else will... the Borg,

00:33:13.257 --> 00:33:15.054
telepathic pitcher plants,
macroviruses.

00:33:15.126 --> 00:33:16.889
The Delta Quadrant
is a death trap.

00:33:16.961 --> 00:33:18.519
What about
the Temporal Prime Directive?

00:33:18.596 --> 00:33:20.231
To hell with it.

00:33:20.298 --> 00:33:24.257
With all due respect,
it's a little presumptuous

00:33:24.335 --> 00:33:26.667
to think you have the right
to change everyone's future.

00:33:26.738 --> 00:33:29.036
From what I've seen,
they'll thank me.

00:33:29.107 --> 00:33:30.768
All you've seen
are bits and pieces.

00:33:30.842 --> 00:33:32.571
You're not getting
the whole picture.

00:33:32.643 --> 00:33:33.701
Really?

00:33:33.778 --> 00:33:35.075
Just what am I missing?

00:33:35.146 --> 00:33:37.580
It's not what, it's who.

00:33:37.648 --> 00:33:40.947
People like Seven of Nine,
a Borg drone

00:33:41.085 --> 00:33:43.246
who'll become a member
of this crew

00:33:43.321 --> 00:33:45.448
after you help her
recover her humanity.

00:33:45.523 --> 00:33:47.923
Or Tom Paris,
a former convict

00:33:47.992 --> 00:33:49.619
who'll be our pilot, chief medic

00:33:49.694 --> 00:33:51.355
and a husband
to B'Elanna Torres.

00:33:51.429 --> 00:33:54.296
That angry woman I just met?

00:33:54.365 --> 00:33:56.458
She's going to be
your Chief Engineer.

00:33:56.534 --> 00:33:59.799
Two crews, Maquis and Starfleet,
are going to become one,

00:33:59.871 --> 00:34:02.567
and they'll make as big
a mark on the Delta Quadrant

00:34:02.640 --> 00:34:04.267
as it'll make on them,

00:34:04.342 --> 00:34:06.333
by protecting people
like the Ocampans,

00:34:06.411 --> 00:34:08.538
curing diseases,
encouraging peace.

00:34:08.613 --> 00:34:10.410
Children like
Naomi and Icheb

00:34:10.481 --> 00:34:12.676
are going to grow up on
this ship and call it home.

00:34:12.750 --> 00:34:14.684
And we'll all be
following a Captain

00:34:14.752 --> 00:34:15.912
who sets a course for Earth

00:34:16.020 --> 00:34:18.284
and never stops believing
that we'll get there.

00:34:19.357 --> 00:34:22.155
Are you going to be
lecturing me like this

00:34:22.226 --> 00:34:23.921
for the next seven years?

00:34:23.995 --> 00:34:27.328
Don't worry, you'll always
get the last word.

00:34:27.398 --> 00:34:29.798
In that case,
let's get back to work.

00:34:32.804 --> 00:34:34.635
So, who is this Seska?

00:34:34.705 --> 00:34:36.297
She was a member of my crew

00:34:36.374 --> 00:34:38.535
who turned out to
be a Cardassian spy.

00:34:38.609 --> 00:34:40.133
She made an alliance
with the Kazon

00:34:40.211 --> 00:34:41.610
and took over the ship.

00:34:41.679 --> 00:34:43.704
It's all right, we got it back.

00:34:43.781 --> 00:34:45.305
Sounds like she's
not going to be

00:34:45.383 --> 00:34:46.748
as cooperative as the others.

00:34:46.818 --> 00:34:49.218
I suggest we take a page
out of your rule book.

00:34:49.287 --> 00:34:51.084
We try diplomacy.

00:34:51.155 --> 00:34:53.783
Fine, but the next page
in that book says

00:34:53.858 --> 00:34:56.952
that when diplomacy fails,
we need a backup plan.

00:34:57.095 --> 00:34:59.689
Something tells me
you already have one.

00:34:59.764 --> 00:35:01.493
We've already injected
the gel packs

00:35:01.566 --> 00:35:02.794
in the other time frames.

00:35:02.867 --> 00:35:04.425
That just leaves the ones here.

00:35:04.502 --> 00:35:07.869
It's in both our
interests to work together.

00:35:08.940 --> 00:35:10.840
I agree.

00:35:10.908 --> 00:35:12.136
Let him go.

00:35:12.210 --> 00:35:14.644
You believe him?

00:35:14.712 --> 00:35:17.772
His story is too
preposterous to be a lie.

00:35:26.491 --> 00:35:29.688
I'll admit, it's an
ingenious solution.

00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:32.820
I'm glad you're cooperating.

00:35:32.897 --> 00:35:36.298
Oh, I believe in cooperation,
as long as it benefits me.

00:35:37.368 --> 00:35:38.835
You know,

00:35:38.903 --> 00:35:41.633
it's true what they say.

00:35:42.707 --> 00:35:45.369
What's that?

00:35:45.443 --> 00:35:48.071
Men just get more distinguished
as they get older.

00:35:48.146 --> 00:35:52.412
A few lines here,
a little gray there.

00:35:52.483 --> 00:35:55.043
It adds character.

00:35:55.119 --> 00:35:57.952
Too bad their minds start to go.

00:35:58.022 --> 00:36:00.650
The last time you were here,
you had that nasty head injury

00:36:00.725 --> 00:36:02.590
and you mumbled
something about

00:36:02.660 --> 00:36:05.060
my taking over the
ship five years ago.

00:36:05.129 --> 00:36:06.153
If that's true,

00:36:06.230 --> 00:36:07.788
then you're from
a future time frame,

00:36:07.865 --> 00:36:09.127
which means that at some point

00:36:09.200 --> 00:36:11.430
your crew is going
to regain control of Voyager.

00:36:11.502 --> 00:36:12.764
I can't allow that to happen.

00:36:12.837 --> 00:36:16.068
Step away from the console.

00:36:19.911 --> 00:36:21.674
An ingenious plan.

00:36:21.746 --> 00:36:23.338
It just needs
a slight modification.

00:36:23.414 --> 00:36:24.438
What are you doing?

00:36:24.515 --> 00:36:27.040
Recalibrating your pulse
to bring the ship

00:36:27.118 --> 00:36:29.416
into temporal sync
with my time frame.

00:36:29.487 --> 00:36:30.351
That's not possible.

00:36:30.421 --> 00:36:31.820
When will you learn

00:36:31.889 --> 00:36:33.720
to stop underestimating me?

00:36:33.791 --> 00:36:35.816
If you make even the
slightest miscalculation,

00:36:35.893 --> 00:36:37.793
you'll destroy the ship
and kill everyone.

00:36:37.862 --> 00:36:39.693
What other choice do I have?

00:36:39.764 --> 00:36:42.096
If I can get Voyager
into my own time frame,

00:36:42.166 --> 00:36:45.033
then I'll be able to ensure
that you never retake the ship.

00:36:48.039 --> 00:36:49.199
Don't worry.

00:36:49.273 --> 00:36:51.366
I won't hurt you.

00:36:51.442 --> 00:36:54.411
You can start fresh with me.

00:36:54.478 --> 00:36:55.809
Sorry.

00:36:55.880 --> 00:36:58.405
That's not the future
I have in mind.

00:36:59.483 --> 00:37:02.281
In that case...

00:37:03.955 --> 00:37:06.116
Good-bye, Chakotay.

00:37:09.961 --> 00:37:12.259
It's too dangerous.

00:37:12.330 --> 00:37:13.262
There are too many variables.

00:37:13.331 --> 00:37:14.457
You're not pleading for your...

00:37:14.532 --> 00:37:15.260
Do it.

00:37:15.333 --> 00:37:16.459
I'm telling you,

00:37:16.534 --> 00:37:18.024
you're endangering
your own life.

00:37:18.102 --> 00:37:19.763
I'm touched by your concern.

00:37:43.894 --> 00:37:44.918
Stop.

00:37:47.732 --> 00:37:49.700
Put down your weapons.

00:37:49.767 --> 00:37:51.598
Don't listen to her.

00:37:51.669 --> 00:37:53.193
Your faithful First Officer

00:37:53.271 --> 00:37:55.330
isn't going to let you die.

00:37:55.406 --> 00:37:56.964
Are you?

00:38:01.012 --> 00:38:03.344
Very clever, Chakotay...

00:38:03.414 --> 00:38:05.006
inoculating them
with your serum.

00:38:05.082 --> 00:38:07.175
Well, now it's time
to inoculate my people,

00:38:07.251 --> 00:38:09.549
so we can have access
to the rest of the ship.

00:38:09.620 --> 00:38:11.212
I won't do that.

00:38:11.289 --> 00:38:13.814
Then you just
lost your Captain.

00:38:20.197 --> 00:38:21.755
Now drop your weapons.

00:38:21.832 --> 00:38:23.129
Thanks.

00:38:33.344 --> 00:38:34.276
Seska and the Kazon

00:38:34.345 --> 00:38:35.642
are secure in the
Jefferies tube.

00:38:35.713 --> 00:38:37.010
The last gel packs?

00:38:37.081 --> 00:38:38.343
They're ready.

00:38:38.416 --> 00:38:40.816
The rest of us should
return to our sections.

00:38:40.885 --> 00:38:42.910
After Chakotay initiates
the warp pulse,

00:38:43.054 --> 00:38:45.249
he should find himself
back at the moment

00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:47.848
Voyager encountered
the chronokinetic surge.

00:38:47.925 --> 00:38:49.893
He's only going to have
a few seconds

00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:51.689
to reset the deflector polarity.

00:38:51.762 --> 00:38:53.229
If the timeline is restored,

00:38:53.297 --> 00:38:56.664
the rest of us should have no
memory of what's happened here.

00:38:56.734 --> 00:38:59.897
So I'd like to thank you now

00:38:59.970 --> 00:39:01.733
for putting
your doubts aside

00:39:01.806 --> 00:39:03.967
and helping me put mine aside
as well.

00:39:04.041 --> 00:39:05.531
Good luck to each of you.

00:39:16.754 --> 00:39:19.052
Mind if I ask you
one last question?

00:39:19.123 --> 00:39:20.420
Will I have to break

00:39:20.491 --> 00:39:23.255
the Temporal Prime
Directive to answer it?

00:39:23.327 --> 00:39:25.318
Maybe... just a little.

00:39:27.465 --> 00:39:30.093
For two people who
started off as enemies,

00:39:30.167 --> 00:39:33.261
it seems we get to know
each other pretty well.

00:39:33.337 --> 00:39:34.804
So I've been wondering...

00:39:36.774 --> 00:39:39.299
just how close do we get?

00:39:42.613 --> 00:39:43.773
Let's just say

00:39:43.848 --> 00:39:47.215
there are some barriers
we never cross.

00:39:53.491 --> 00:39:55.959
See you in the future.

00:40:06.137 --> 00:40:07.399
Ensign?

00:40:07.471 --> 00:40:09.666
Chakotay should be
initiating the pulse

00:40:09.740 --> 00:40:11.708
in ten seconds.

00:40:13.744 --> 00:40:18.909
Five, four, three, two...

00:40:29.794 --> 00:40:31.887
Reroute main power
to the deflector

00:40:31.962 --> 00:40:33.190
and set the polarity

00:40:33.264 --> 00:40:35.061
to the frequency
I'm inputting.

00:40:35.132 --> 00:40:36.497
Why?

00:40:36.567 --> 00:40:38.626
Have you ever heard
of a lightning rod?

00:40:38.702 --> 00:40:41.296
In about three seconds,
we're going to need one.

00:40:46.043 --> 00:40:47.977
What is it?

00:40:48.078 --> 00:40:50.512
I don't know.

00:40:50.581 --> 00:40:52.173
Main power's being rerouted

00:40:52.249 --> 00:40:53.614
to the deflector dish.

00:40:53.684 --> 00:40:54.946
Who gave that order?

00:41:01.425 --> 00:41:03.723
Damage?

00:41:03.794 --> 00:41:06.854
The deflector's been burned out,

00:41:06.931 --> 00:41:08.455
but we're okay.

00:41:19.777 --> 00:41:21.176
Do you mind telling me

00:41:21.245 --> 00:41:23.406
why B'Elanna burned out
the deflector dish?

00:41:23.481 --> 00:41:25.244
Actually, I ordered her
to do it.

00:41:25.316 --> 00:41:26.510
Why?

00:41:26.584 --> 00:41:28.950
Trust me, it was better
than the alternative.

00:41:29.053 --> 00:41:30.953
Which was what, exactly?

00:41:31.088 --> 00:41:32.350
I can't tell you.

00:41:32.423 --> 00:41:33.822
Why not?

00:41:33.891 --> 00:41:35.756
The Temporal Prime Directive.

00:41:36.827 --> 00:41:38.658
B'Elanna's already got a team

00:41:38.729 --> 00:41:39.787
working on repairs.

00:41:39.864 --> 00:41:42.025
What do you say
we finish our dinner?

00:41:46.170 --> 00:41:47.728
Forget particle fountains

00:41:47.805 --> 00:41:49.397
and subspace inversions.

00:41:49.473 --> 00:41:51.464
There isn't
an anomaly scarier

00:41:51.542 --> 00:41:53.874
than a thunderstorm
on the plains,

00:41:53.944 --> 00:41:56.412
especially when
you're six years old.

00:41:56.480 --> 00:41:58.880
I remember watching
a bolt of lightning

00:41:58.949 --> 00:42:01.645
split an oak tree in
my grandfather's yard.

00:42:01.719 --> 00:42:04.119
I'd climbed it just
a few hours before.

00:42:04.188 --> 00:42:05.815
Good timing.

00:42:05.890 --> 00:42:07.289
So what would have happened

00:42:07.358 --> 00:42:09.451
if you hadn't turned
our deflector dish

00:42:09.527 --> 00:42:10.653
into a lightning rod?

00:42:10.728 --> 00:42:12.457
We've been down
this road before.

00:42:12.530 --> 00:42:13.792
Have we?

00:42:13.864 --> 00:42:17.300
You wanting answers to questions
you shouldn't ask.

00:42:17.368 --> 00:42:19.268
But something did happen...

00:42:19.336 --> 00:42:22.396
outside the normal
space-time continuum.

00:42:26.810 --> 00:42:28.038
It's strange

00:42:28.112 --> 00:42:30.580
thinking there's a piece
of your life

00:42:30.648 --> 00:42:32.741
you don't know anything about.

00:42:32.816 --> 00:42:34.943
Sounds a lot like the future.

00:42:35.085 --> 00:42:36.313
Any predictions?

00:42:36.387 --> 00:42:40.551
Only that in a few minutes,
this bottle will be empty.

00:42:40.624 --> 00:42:42.615
Then maybe you should go
to the cargo bay

00:42:42.693 --> 00:42:43.751
and grab another one.

00:42:43.827 --> 00:42:46.557
How do you know
that's where I keep it?

00:42:46.630 --> 00:42:48.621
Oh, I can't tell you.

00:42:48.699 --> 00:42:49.893
Why not?

00:42:49.967 --> 00:42:52.401
Temporal Prime Directive.
